// The other unit of 1170_region_loop_laps_across_units: what the loops there
// call -- a parser making a record and its fields for every line, a chain
// grown by one link, entries a cache keeps, and a check that throws.
namespace LoopUnits;

public sealed class Field
{
    public readonly string Text;
    public readonly int Value;

    public Field(string text, int value) { Text = text; Value = value; }
}

public sealed class Record
{
    public readonly List<Field> Fields = new List<Field>();
    public int[] Sums;

    public Record(int width) { Sums = new int[width]; }
}

public sealed class Entry
{
    public readonly int[] Values;

    public Entry(int n) { Values = new int[n]; }
}

public sealed class Link
{
    public readonly Link? Next;
    public readonly int V;

    public Link(int v, Link? next) { V = v; Next = next; }
}

public static class Parser
{
    public static Record Parse(int line, int width)
    {
        Record r = new Record(width);
        for (int k = 0; k < width; k++)
        {
            int v = line * 7 + k;
            r.Fields.Add(new Field("f" + v.ToString(), v));
            r.Sums[k] = v;
        }
        return r;
    }

    public static Link Chain(int v, Link? next) => new Link(v, next);

    public static Entry Make(int v, int n)
    {
        Entry e = new Entry(n);
        for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) e.Values[k] = v + k;
        return e;
    }

    public static int Check(Record r, int bad)
    {
        if (r.Fields.Count == bad) throw new InvalidOperationException("bad record of " + bad.ToString());
        return r.Fields.Count;
    }
}

public static class Cache
{
    static readonly List<Entry> _kept = new List<Entry>();

    public static void Keep(Entry e) => _kept.Add(e);

    public static int Count => _kept.Count;

    public static long Total()
    {
        long s = 0;
        foreach (Entry e in _kept)
            foreach (int v in e.Values) s += v;
        return s;
    }
}
